groups.push(['Corrupted lands',[
 ['corruption_blood_fungus','Blood-fungus corrupted valley','scene','16:9','A visibly sick, grey, dying woodland valley overtaken by a spreading crimson fungal blight, inspired by the oppressive corrupted-nature atmosphere of Drova while keeping the supplied Meridius painting and elevated battlefield camera. Broad asymmetrical shelves of dark wine-red fungus climb dead trunks; smaller rust-red caps and pale branching mycelium spread across earth and exposed roots. A shallow winding stream is polluted with muted reddish-brown fungal runoff, dark silt and a few oily-looking patches; this is stained water, not literal blood. The entire valley looks poisoned: exhausted ash-grey soil, charcoal-grey wet rot, sparse collapsed grey grass, withered bushes and stripped pallid dying trees. Keep crimson and wine-red fungus as the only strong colour. Remove healthy golden meadow, lush green foliage and pleasant warm sunlight. Use dim cold overcast light, readable shadow and thin dirty-grey mist. Water is murky opaque grey-green with dark silt and rust-red fungal scum, never clean bright blue. Collapsed rotten logs, cracked pallid bark and shrivelled dead grey vegetation tell the history of the infestation. The land itself is visibly dying, rather than a healthy forest with decorative mushrooms. Keep two wide dry routes and a shallow crossing legible between fungal colonies. Rich tactile detail in strong grouped shapes, beautiful ominous colour contrast, no giant central mushroom blocking the whole image. No people, corpses, gore, organs, monsters, neon glow, fog curtain or UI.'],
 ['corruption_root_rot','Black root-rot marsh','scene','16:9','A once-green woodland hollow corrupted by black root rot. Great twisted charcoal-brown roots break through damp peat and wrap around dead stumps, while low shelves of ivory-grey fungus grow from split bark. Small stagnant pools of dark green-brown water have restrained ochre films and collapsed reeds; branching drainage channels connect them naturally. Surviving mossy forest at one far edge gives way to leafless trees, pale dying grass and exposed rotten wood. A raised but naturally rounded dry bank and an old worn cart track provide two clear crossing routes. Ominous through physical decay and beautiful layered painting rather than neon magical effects. Keep the complete elevated no-horizon battlefield composition, continuous ground, rich texture and readable shadows. No people, skeletons, monsters, literal blood, active smoke, flames or UI.'],
 ['corruption_crystal','Violet crystal blight','scene','16:9','A natural rocky meadow slowly poisoned by an invasive mineral blight. Unequal clusters of dull amethyst and smoky-violet crystals grow from existing rock fractures and thread through exposed tree roots, with fine pale mineral crusts staining soil along connected shallow seep channels. Nearby trees have bleached bark, sparse dusty-purple leaves and broken dead limbs; healthy olive woodland survives at the far boundary. Strong organic rounded hills contrast with angular crystal growths. Keep crystals mostly at the edges and on one low ridge, leaving a broad winding dirt route and open central ground for formations. Rich painted stone and timber detail, restrained purple-versus-ochre palette, readable physical terrain. Crystals reflect ordinary light with no neon emission or magical beam. No floating islands, huge central crystal tower, people, creatures, explosions, fog curtain or UI.'],
 ['corruption_ash','Ash-choked corrupted forest','scene','16:9','A haunting forest valley exhausted by a creeping grey blight: ash-coloured dust settles in shallow gullies, mature trees stand as twisted pale skeletal silhouettes, dead roots cross eroded banks and dry blackened trunks lie among cracked earth. Rounded islands of sickly straw grass and small chalk-white fungal crusts interrupt the grey soil. A former stream is completely dry, showing dusty sediment rings and smooth dark stones. At the upper perimeter a small remaining green woodland patch reveals the advancing corruption boundary. An abandoned worn road bends around the largest fallen trunk and crosses the dry channel at a shallow ford; keep routes wide and believable. Powerful layered shapes, detailed weathered wood, muted bone-grey, charcoal, ochre and deep cool shadow, clear elevated isometric no-horizon view. This is old quiet devastation: no burning trees, active fire, smoke, lava, people, creatures or UI.'],
]]);
groups.push(['Northern European forest comparisons', [
 ['road_forest_northern_clear','Thick northern forest — clear daylight','scene','16:9','A deeply wooded northern European landscape with a naturally worn cart road winding between imposing mature Norway spruce and Scots pine, a few silver birches, and occasional old broadleaf trees in the lower moist ground. Tall irregular canopies overlap in several layers; massive textured trunks and hanging boughs make the forest feel old and extensive. Dense moss, fern colonies, tangled bilberry-like low shrubs, exposed roots, fallen branches and decaying nurse logs occupy the forest floor, with pockets of rock and damp earth. Thick wild woodland continues on both sides and into the distance, never isolated decorative tree clumps around a manicured lawn. Keep the road and a few natural clearings legible at the established elevated isometric camera, with believable ruts, turning arcs, soft drainage and grass only where traffic is light. This is the CLEAR DAYLIGHT comparison requested by the user: natural neutral daylight, deep green foliage, readable cool shadows, no fog, no mist and no dramatic darkening. Show the richer northern forest character through tree species, height, density and untamed ground. No people, creatures, camps, torches, UI or horizon.'],
 ['road_forest_northern_fog','Imposing northern forest — dark and foggy','scene','16:9','An imposing old northern European forest with a winding natural cart road, towering Norway spruce and Scots pine, scattered pale birch trunks and a few immense gnarled broadleaf trees. Dense uneven layers of overlapping crowns and great trunks rise above tangled undergrowth, mossy boulders, exposed roots and fallen decaying timber. The forest feels vast and self-grown, with no clipped lawns, ornamental clumps or regular tree spacing. Dark moss-green, bottle-green and cool blue-green shadows, restrained natural highlights under overcast daylight. Drifting low grey fog winds among trunks and gathers in hollows; layered atmospheric mist gives depth to the far forest, while the nearest road, roots and branches remain sharply readable. Preserve a believable quiet cart road with worn paired ruts, irregular soft verges, modest drainage and natural turns around terrain. Make the trees imposing in scale without blocking the entire route. The elevated isometric camera looks down into a continuous forest landscape with no sky or horizon. No figures, creatures, torches, neon glow, UI or floating diorama.'],
]]);
const northernForestDirection = 'LATEST WOODLAND DIRECTION: Wherever this location contains forest, make it imposing, thick and northern European: tall irregular spruce and Scots pine, silver birch and occasional mature broadleaf trees, overlapping woodland layers, dark natural greens, mossy stones, ferns, tangled low growth, fallen timber and uneven self-grown edges. Keep nature wild and extensive rather than park-like, neatly spaced or clipped. Use subdued cool daylight and drifting low fog between trunks and in hollows, keeping nearby routes and structures readable. This woodland atmosphere supersedes earlier golden park-like vegetation or a blanket ban on mist. Preserve the requested biome and open areas; do not fill camp interiors, drill grounds, roads or deforested clearings with new trees. Camp layouts and buildings remain as approved. Keep the original painterly rendering and elevated camera.';
const nightBases = groups.flatMap(([,rows])=>rows).filter(([id,,kind])=>kind==='scene'||['orc_pit','orc_pit_fortified','dragon_lair','dragon_lair_snow'].includes(id));
groups.push(['Night locations', nightBases.map(([id,title,kind,aspect,subject])=>[`${id}_night`, `${title.replace(/^Sunlit /,'')} — night`, kind, aspect, subject])]);
const nightStyle = `REFERENCE ROLES: Attach ONLY the matching reviewed daytime image. It is the exact source to edit, including its geometry, camera, framing, scale, structures, paths, object placement and painted material style. Make a faithful NIGHT LIGHTING EDIT of this single image. The supplied Meridius style references are already embodied in this accepted source; do not introduce elements from other images.

ART DIRECTION: Keep layered painted foliage, textured worn timber and stone, restrained crisp brush shapes and all local details. No glossy 3D, photorealism, low-poly simplification, thick cartoon outlines or pixelation filter.

NIGHT LIGHT: Remove warm sunlight and daytime light shafts. Illuminate from upper left with gentle cool silver-blue moonlight and soft blue-green ambient fill. The scene must clearly read as night while every route, slope, entrance and material stays legible. Preserve hue differences between grass, stone, timber and snow; do not apply a flat blue filter or crush shadows to black. No visible sky, moon disc, stars, fog curtain, magical glow, fires, torches, troops or added objects. Existing town windows may have a very restrained warm interior glow. Preserve existing empty site entrances and roads.`;

export const pilotOrder = ['tree_oak', 'battlefield_meadow', 'house_cottage', 'ruin_arch', 'orc_pit', 'dragon_lair'];

export function entries() {
  return groups.flatMap(([group, rows]) => rows.map(([id, title, kind, aspect, subject]) => {
    const night=id.endsWith('_night');
    const wide=id.startsWith('road_');
    const northernFog=id.startsWith('road_forest_northern_fog');
    const selectedNightStyle=nightStyle.replace('Existing town windows may have a very restrained warm interior glow.', id.startsWith('camp_')||id==='battlefield_town_night' ? 'Only windows or tent openings ALREADY PRESENT in the attached daytime source may have restrained warm interior light. Do not add any building, tent, window or light fixture.' : 'Do not add buildings, cabins, shelters, tents, windows, lamps or warm lights. Keep every wilderness area free of settlement and artificial lighting. Preserve only structures that already exist in the attached daytime source.');
    const format=wide ? 'FORMAT: One continuous 16:9 landscape. Elevated isometric camera, zoomed well out, parallel axes, no visible sky or horizon. Long connected roads and verges occupy about 40 percent of the image with forest on both sides. Quiet details on the movement lanes, natural continuous terrain, no square tile edges, floating base, border, troops, creatures, labels, grid or UI.' : formats[kind];
    return {
      id, title, group, kind, aspect, quality: '2K', optional: kind === 'texture',
      filename: `${id}__take-01.png`, referenceCount:night?1:2,
      ...(night?{baseId:id.slice(0,-6)}:{}),
      prompt: night ? `MERIDIUS TERRAIN ART — ${title.toUpperCase()}\n\n${selectedNightStyle}\n\nPRESERVATION: Keep this exact accepted composition. Preserve every road bend, tree, stump, rock, bank, building, tent, gate and empty entrance in its current position and size. Preserve existing fog or clear conditions, dry channels and water boundaries. Change lighting only; do not add, remove or redesign objects.\n\nFORMAT: Keep the original ${aspect} canvas, elevated isometric camera, exact crop and complete framing.${kind!=='scene'?' Keep the perfectly uniform magenta extraction background unchanged; only the site itself receives night lighting. Do not add a horizon, terrain outside the isolated footprint or a shadow on the background.':' Preserve continuous terrain to all four image edges, with no sky, horizon, border or floating base.'} No figures, creatures, torches, UI, text or watermark.` :`MERIDIUS TERRAIN ART — ${title.toUpperCase()}\n\n${night?selectedNightStyle:style}\n\n${night?'PRESERVATION: Keep the exact matching daytime composition from image 3; change lighting only. The described location is:':'SUBJECT:'} ${subject}\n\n${format}${night&&kind!=='scene'?' Preserve the perfectly uniform magenta extraction background unchanged; only the site itself receives night lighting. Keep the complete silhouette and at least 10 percent padding.':''}${kind==='scene'||id.startsWith('street_')?'\n\n'+naturalLandscapeDirection:''}${!night&&kind==='scene'&&id!=='road_forest_northern_clear'?'\n\n'+northernForestDirection:''}${id==='road_forest_northern_clear'?'\n\nFINAL CLEAR-DAY OVERRIDE: This particular comparison has denser, taller northern European forest under neutral natural daylight. No fog, no mist, no gloomy weather treatment; forest character and density are the only intended atmospheric changes.':''}${northernFog&&!night?'\n\nFINAL DENSITY OVERRIDE: This is a forest-dominated composition. Dense mature woodland occupies about 80 percent of the image; the modest road and its irregular verges occupy the remaining 20 percent, overriding the earlier generic road-space percentage. Tall interlocking crowns, trunks at several depths, tight understory and low drifting fog enclose the route. No broad meadow, large sunny lawn, isolated decorative groves, golden sunset or empty park clearing. Keep the road readable as it bends through this immense forest.':''}${night?'\n\nFINAL NIGHT OVERRIDE: Any daylight or warm-sun description above is descriptive of the daytime source only. Replace sunlight with readable cool moonlight while retaining the exact composition and existing fog or clear conditions of the attached daytime source. Do not redesign its forest.':''}`,
    };
  })).map(item => {
    if (item.id.startsWith('corruption_') && !item.baseId) {
      item.prompt += '\n\nFINAL CORRUPTION ATMOSPHERE: The land itself is visibly unhealthy, decaying and poisoned. Follow this corruption type\'s specific materials and colours over the healthy golden grass or sunlight of the style references. Use subdued overcast lighting and exhausted vegetation around the infection; healthy woodland is confined to any explicitly described far boundary. No pleasant golden meadow or warm scenic glow. Preserve readable terrain, detailed painting and the original elevated camera.';
    }
    return item;
  });
}
